+# Patch 0028: in-app help, part 1 (B7a): format, checker, build, first three pages
+
+Items: B7 (started). Status: `[x]` done and tested in my sandbox (pure logic, `tsc`), `[ ]` needs you.
+
+## Design decisions (read these, tell me if one is wrong)
+- **One source.** Pages are Markdown files in `help/`. The app and the docs Worker read the same generated `help/help.json`, so they cannot drift. Git history is the version history; the file also carries a content fingerprint (`version`).
+- **Three depths in one file.** `## Basic`, `## Deep`, `## Advanced` sections. **Choosing a depth shows it plus the ones above it** (Deep = Basic + Deep). I chose this so nobody reads two copies of a page. Say if you would rather see only the level you picked.
+- **Nested and interlinked.** Every page has a `parent` (the folders-in-folders tree) and `[[page-id]]` links; each page also shows "pages that link here". Contents lists are built from `parent`, never written by hand, so a new page appears in the right place automatically.
+- **A page cannot be wrong in structure.** The build refuses a set with a dead link, a missing parent, a parent loop, a missing Basic section, an unclosed code block, a stray `##`, or a mermaid block with no diagram type.
+- **No new package, no native rebuild.** Everything in this patch is pure TypeScript plus Markdown.
+
+## Steps
+1. [x] Read the repo (latest commit is patch 0027), DEV_NOTES and PROGRESS. Baseline: 282 tests pass.
+2. [x] `src/lib/helpDocs.ts` (pure): header reader, depth sections (fence-aware), links (fence and inline-code aware), `selectDepth`, `validatePages`, `buildIndex`/`trail`, `searchPages`, `diagramBlocks`, bundle (`makeBundle`, `readBundle`, `contentVersion`).
+3. [x] `scripts/build-help.ts` + `npm run help:build` / `npm run help:check`.
+4. [x] `help/help.json` (generated) and `help/README.md` (the writer's guide: format, what each depth is for, link and flowchart rules, style).
+5. [x] Pages: `start` (Help home and how depth works), `sales` (Checkout: the main screen), `sales/cart-and-prices` (the cart and the four-step price order). Every Advanced claim checked against `Checkout.tsx`, `CartPane.tsx`, `cartOps.ts`, `pricing.ts`, `selectors.ts`, `store.ts`, `invoiceRows.ts`.
+6. [x] `tests/helpdocs.test.ts` (23 tests): header, sections, fences, depth, ids, links, every validation rule, index and trail, search, bundle, and the real `help/` pages (no problems, all reachable from `start`, `help.json` current). A mutation check confirmed the inline-code link rule is really tested.
+7. [x] `docs/PROGRESS.md`: patch log row, the full B7 page plan with a checkbox per page, new item N21.
+8. [x] Total tests 305 pass; `tsc --noEmit` clean.
+9. [ ] You: read the three pages (they are plain Markdown for now) and tell me about anything wrong or unclear, in tone or in fact (N21).
+
+## Deliberately not in this patch
+- The in-app Help screen (0029) and the docs Worker (0030). Until 0029 the pages are only files.
+- The pages mention "More ▸ Help". That entry arrives in 0029.
